cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference Terse in research or writing, please cite it as below."
title: "Terse — on-device token optimization and AI coding agent monitoring"
abstract: >-
  Terse is an on-device AI agent butler for macOS and Windows. It compresses
  prompts 40-70% before they reach the API, live-monitors eight AI coding
  agents (Claude Code, Cursor, OpenAI Codex, GitHub Copilot CLI, Cline,
  Windsurf, OpenClaw, Aider), enforces spend ceilings with a budget circuit
  breaker that pauses or kills a runaway agent before its next API call,
  manages MCP servers with security risk scoring, and diagnoses token waste.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Terse AI"
    website: "https://www.terseai.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Terse-AI/terseai"
url: "https://www.terseai.org"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - token optimization
  - prompt compression
  - AI coding agents
  - Claude Code
  - Cursor
  - LLM cost reduction
  - Model Context Protocol
  - on-device
